(Q2) converse pairing of multiplicities
  ok   N(n,h) = SC(n,h) (mod 2) for every n <= 9 and h (non-self-converse classes pair with their converses; PROVED)
  ok   the same for strong classes: P_d(z) = SC_d(z) (mod 2) coefficientwise
  ok   even n <= 8: every self-converse class has H = 1 (mod 4) (THM-791 with a fixed-point-free anti-involution)
  ok   hence at even n every value H = 3 (mod 4) is attained by an even number of classes
  ok   n = 5: 3 uniquely attained values, all self-converse: 1(|Aut| 1), 11(|Aut| 1), 13(|Aut| 1)
  ok   n = 6: 2 uniquely attained values, all self-converse: 1(|Aut| 1), 41(|Aut| 1)
  ok   n = 7: 12 uniquely attained values, all self-converse: 1(|Aut| 1), 61(|Aut| 1), 85(|Aut| 1), 87(|Aut| 1), 125(|Aut| 1), 127(|Aut| 1), 147(|Aut| 1), 155(|Aut| 1), 157(|Aut| 1), 171(|Aut| 3, regular), 175(|Aut| 7, regular), 189(|Aut| 21, regular)
  ok   n = 8: 3 uniquely attained values, all self-converse: 1(|Aut| 1), 629(|Aut| 1), 637(|Aut| 1)
  ok   n = 9: 26 uniquely attained values, all self-converse: 1(|Aut| 1), 2891(|Aut| 1), 2917(|Aut| 1), 2919(|Aut| 1), 2931(|Aut| 3), 2959(|Aut| 1), 2963(|Aut| 1), 2979(|Aut| 1), 3079(|Aut| 1), 3081(|Aut| 1), 3083(|Aut| 1), 3085(|Aut| 1), 3095(|Aut| 1), 3101(|Aut| 1) ...
(Q3) late primes and the late seven
     (p, first order whose strong range holds an odd multiple of p, first order with p | H strong): [(7, 6, 7), (107, 7, 8), (149, 7, 8), (163, 7, 8), (167, 7, 8), (173, 7, 8), (179, 7, 8), (181, 7, 8)]
  ok   p = 7 is late: odd multiples of 7 (21, 35) enter the strong range [15, 45] at order 6, but 7 | H first at order 7; 3, 5, 11, ..., 31 divide a strong count at the first order whose range allows it; the other late primes (107, 149, ...) sit above the order-7 holes near its maximum
  ok   no tournament with n <= 6 has 7 | H (FINITE-EXACT); so 7 | H(T) forces a strong component of order >= 7 with 7 | H (PROVED from multiplicativity)
  ok   at n = 7 every tournament with 7 | H is strong; the multiples of 7 attained: 35x2, 49x7, 77x10, 91x15, 105x4, 133x6, 147x1, 175x1, 189x1
     n = 7: odd multiples of 7 below the maximum that are missing: [7, 21, 63, 119, 161]; all odd holes: [7, 21, 63, 107, 119, 149, 161, 163, 165, 167, 169, 173, 177, 179, 181, 183, 185, 187]
     n = 7: holes in (45, 150): [63, 107, 119, 149] -> multiples of 7: [63, 119], primes: [107, 149]
     n = 7: labelled fraction with 7 | H = 0.1086; among strong labelled = 0.1358  (1/7 = 0.1429)
     n = 8: labelled fraction with 7 | H = 0.1377; among strong labelled = 0.1409  (1/7 = 0.1429)
     n = 9: labelled fraction with 7 | H = 0.1420; among strong labelled = 0.1422  (1/7 = 0.1429)
